# Today I Learned — 2026-05-06

Tip: use structuredClone for safe, fast deep clones of many built-ins (Date, RegExp, Map, Set, ArrayBuffer, TypedArray, Blob, etc.). It does not clone functions, DOM nodes, or preserve custom class prototypes — use a custom serializer or library for those cases.

```js
// Example deep-clone helper with graceful fallback
// structuredClone is available in modern browsers & Node; fallback uses JSON (limited)
function deepClone<T>(value: T): T {
  if (typeof structuredClone === "function") return structuredClone(value);
  // JSON fallback: works for plain objects/arrays with JSON-safe values
  return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(value));
}

/*
Usage:
  const original = { d: new Date(), s: new Set([1,2]), n: null };
  const copy = deepClone(original);
Note: copy will preserve Date/Set with structuredClone, but fallback will not.
*/
```